# Improved AMP: a lock trig (a trig without a note: FUNC + the trig key in GRID RECORDING) is not faded
# for, and one with RTRG on gives a running retrig series its own rate, whose strikes are faded for.
# HLD 57 holds each strike into the next; each take plays the pattern three times (3 hits).
# `lk`: note trigs on steps 1 and 3, a lock trig on step 2, ENV RESET AMP: 3 dips (before step 3 each
# time); a fade before the lock trig would silence the voice until step 3 (6 hits, no dip).
# `lr`: a trig with a retrig lock on step 1 (the kit's RATE and LEN: 1/16 and 1/4 here, strikes on steps
# 1 to 4) and a lock trig on step 3 with RTRG on at RATE 1/32 (UP in the retrig menu: 1/16, 1/20, 1/24,
# 1/32). From step 3 on the series strikes every 62.5 ms until its length ends at step 5: at 0, 125, 250,
# 312.5, 375 and 437.5 ms as the module counts it, 5 dips a time, the shortest 62.5 ms apart. At OFF: no
# dip, and the first hit is as long as at AMP (to 60 ms).
# `lr` is also what shows that the gesture places a lock trig on the unit: nothing on the screen does.
# Expected from the module's README and code and from stock's manual; not yet run on the unit.
# The retrig menus' screens are checked against their references. The BD track needs a sound that rings
# with the AMP envelope open.
# Changes the tempo, the BD track's AMP page and its ENV RESET in the active kit, and the BD track of the
# active pattern, which it clears; ends at 120 BPM, ENV RESET OFF, HLD 0, the track empty.
name: improved-amp-prefade-locktrig
state: changes
transport: any
target: unit

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
# Tempo to 120.0: down to the bottom (30.0), then 90 BPM up, a step of the tempo screen's LEVEL being 1 BPM.
key TEMPO
enc LEVEL -127 x64
nudge LEVEL +21 per 6 x4
nudge LEVEL +6 per 6
wait 500
screen tempo
expect tempo == ref region 40 15 88 33
key NO
key AMP
cc 78 0
cc 79 57
cc 80 55
cc 81 0
cc 82 0
cc 83 0
cc 10 64
cc 7 100
hold FUNC
wait 300
key MUTE
release FUNC
key UP x4
key DOWN x4
key YES
key UP x8
key DOWN x2
key LEFT x3
key RIGHT
wait 500
screen er1
expect er1 == ref region 39 26 82 11
key NO x3
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
key FUNC+PLAY
wait 800
key T1
key T3
hold FUNC
wait 300
key T2
release FUNC
wait 300
key RECORD
wait 300
audio lk BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
key FUNC+PLAY
wait 800
key T1
hold FUNC
wait 300
key T3
release FUNC
wait 300
hold T1
wait 300
key RTRG
wait 400
key RTRG
wait 400
screen rt1
release T1
wait 300
expect rt1 == ref region 13 19 104 28
hold T3
wait 300
key RTRG
wait 400
key RTRG
wait 400
key UP x3
wait 400
screen rt3
release T3
wait 300
expect rt3 == ref region 13 19 104 28
expect rt3 != rt1 region 13 19 104 28
key RECORD
wait 300
audio lr BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
hold FUNC
wait 300
key MUTE
release FUNC
key UP x4
key DOWN x4
key YES
key UP x8
key DOWN x2
key LEFT x3
wait 500
screen er0
expect er0 == ref region 39 26 82 11
key NO x3
wait 300
audio lroff BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
key FUNC+PLAY
wait 800
key RECORD
cc 79 0

expect lk.hits == 3
expect lk.dips == 3
expect lr.hits == 3
expect lr.dips == 15
expect lr.gapmin == 62.5 within 4
expect lroff.hits == 3
expect lroff.dips == 0
expect lr.len20 > lroff.len20 - 60
expect lr.len20 < lroff.len20 + 60
